# shellcheck shell=bash
# shellcheck disable=SC2034  # Vars are consumed by Kamal externally.
#
# Kamal reads this with dotenv (NOT bash): plain assignment + $(...) work, but bash
# default-expansion ${VAR:-default} does not. Shared by BOTH apps in this repo
# (deploy.coordinator.yml + deploy.signer.yml), so ALL THREE SOPS sources below must exist
# before EITHER `kamal deploy` — Kamal evaluates the whole file regardless of which app it
# is deploying, and a `sops -d` on a missing file aborts the deploy.
#
# Secrets are pulled from the sibling private infra repo's SOPS files (two levels up:
# .../Develop/VIZ/viz-gateway → .../Develop/infra). Nothing secret is written to disk.
INFRA=../../infra

# GHCR pull/push PAT (write:packages). Shared across every axveer app.
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(sops -d --extract '["docker_registry_password"]' "$INFRA/secrets/shared.enc.yaml")

# toncenter API key — single-sourced from the coordinator app's SOPS file and reused by the
# signer app (both env.secret blocks reference GRAM_API_KEY).
GRAM_API_KEY=$(sops -d --extract '["gram_api_key"]' "$INFRA/secrets/apps/viz-gateway-coordinator.enc.yaml")

# Passphrase that unseals op-1's keystore.mainnet.json at signer boot. Only the signer app
# references it; it is still extracted on a coordinator deploy (see header) — harmless.
# SOPS key is fed_keystore_passWORD (not …passphrase) so it matches .sops.yaml's
# encrypted_regex (…_password) and is actually encrypted at rest; the Kamal env var it
# feeds is still FED_KEYSTORE_PASSPHRASE (what config.ts reads).
FED_KEYSTORE_PASSPHRASE=$(sops -d --extract '["fed_keystore_password"]' "$INFRA/secrets/apps/viz-gateway-signer.enc.yaml")

# gram.gate MEMO private key (WIF) — decrypts '#'-encrypted peg-in memos. NON-fund-controlling
# (memo role is not in any authority; a leak is a privacy exposure, not custody — AUDIT.md §8),
# so it lives as a SOPS secret env like GRAM_API_KEY rather than in the keystore. Single-sourced
# from the coordinator SOPS file and reused by BOTH apps (coordinator's viz-watcher role decrypts
# to enqueue the destination; the signer re-decrypts at F2). Must exist before EITHER deploy.
VIZ_MEMO_WIF_GRAM=$(sops -d --extract '["gram_gate_memo_key"]' "$INFRA/secrets/apps/viz-gateway-coordinator.enc.yaml")

# Bearer token for the coordinator's POST /submit (PR #129). Shared ONLY between the
# coordinator web role (verifies) and the dispatcher role (sends) — same app env; the
# signer app never calls /submit and does not reference it.
COORDINATOR_SUBMIT_TOKEN=$(sops -d --extract '["coordinator_submit_token"]' "$INFRA/secrets/apps/viz-gateway-coordinator.enc.yaml")

# On-call push channel for notifyStaff (fail-closed pauses, drift, wedged delivery). A
# Telegram sendMessage URL with chat_id in the query — @gateway/log reshapes the alert to
# Telegram's {chat_id, text} for this URL form (generic endpoints get the JSON shape). It
# embeds the bot token, hence a SOPS secret. Unset = alerts are file-only (three production
# pauses sat unalerted that way; keep it set).
# SOPS key is staff_webhook_URI (not …_url) so it matches .sops.yaml's encrypted_regex
# (…_uri) and is actually encrypted at rest; the env var stays STAFF_WEBHOOK_URL (what
# @gateway/log reads).
STAFF_WEBHOOK_URL=$(sops -d --extract '["staff_webhook_uri"]' "$INFRA/secrets/apps/viz-gateway-coordinator.enc.yaml")
